 summary="Diabetic foot disease results from peripheral neuropathy, peripheral artery disease (PAD) and deformity, which together let unnoticed trauma become an ulcer. Loss of protective sensation (LOPS) removes the warning of pain; PAD impairs healing; infection spreads along tissue planes and to bone. Infection is diagnosed clinically and graded by severity (IWGDF/IDSA), which sets the antibiotic route, spectrum and need for surgery. Antibiotics do not work without wound care, debridement, offloading and good glucose control (ICMR STW).",
