  ("Infection grade 1–2 (IWGDF/IDSA Table 1)", "Grade 1 uninfected; Grade 2 mild: at least two local signs (swelling or induration, erythema 0.5 to under 2 cm, tenderness, warmth, pus), skin and subcutaneous tissue only, no systemic signs."),
  ("Infection grade 3–4 (IWGDF/IDSA Table 1)", "Grade 3 moderate: erythema 2 cm or more or deeper than subcutaneous tissue, no systemic signs. Grade 4 severe: with two or more SIRS criteria. Add (O) if bone is involved."),
